## 4. The complete production workflow

This is the heart of ST: every Director should be capable of taking a content idea through the entire production lifecycle.

### 01

IDEA & PLANNING

Find a topic, define the audience, format, duration, language, and production deadline.

### 02

RESEARCH & VERIFICATION

Collect credible sources, validate claims, assess rights, and flag uncertainty.

### 03

STORY & SCRIPT

Create the outline, scenes, narration, dialogue, character arcs, and episode structure.

### 04

CHARACTER & VISUAL DESIGN

Define character references, locations, scene composition, visual style, and continuity.

### 05

VOICE & AUDIO

Generate or record narration and dialogue; prepare emotion, pronunciation, BGM, SFX, and music.

### 06

VISUALS & MOTION

Generate or assemble scenes, animation, camera movement, transitions, and motion effects.

### 07

VIDEO ASSEMBLY

Use FFmpeg to combine visuals, voice, music, sound effects, captions, and transitions.

### 08

TECHNICAL & CONTENT QC

Use FFprobe and automated checks to verify duration, stream integrity, audio/video, captions, and package completeness.

### 09

FINAL CONTENT PACKAGE

Create the main episode, two standalone content Shorts/Reels, one standalone brand-promotion Reel, thumbnails, subtitles, metadata, and evidence.

### 10

OWNER APPROVAL

Present the exact artifacts, destinations, metadata, and disclosures for approval.

### 11

PUBLISH & VERIFY

Submit only to authorized platforms; capture genuine responses and publication receipts.

### 12

ANALYTICS & LEARNING

Collect actual performance metrics, evaluate results, and propose the next improvements.

### How the workflow should behave

- A failed provider should trigger a permitted fallback, a retry, or an honest waiting state—not fabricated success.
- Every long-running stage should support durable checkpoints, heartbeats, retries and idempotency.
- If narration or required media is missing, the package must remain incomplete.
- A video cannot pass merely because an MP4 file exists. It must pass technical checks and content-specific QC.
- Publishing success must be based on a genuine platform response and persisted receipt.
- Analytics must come from real observations, not invented numbers.

This is how ST moves from an AI script generator to an auditable production system.

