## 6. Hermes — the brain of the production house

Hermes is intended to be more than a chatbot or dashboard. It is ST's central orchestration and management layer.

Its responsibilities include:

1. Planning: identify production priorities and coordinate episode schedules.
2. Resource management: assign available workers, select eligible providers, respect quota limits and avoid unnecessary paid usage.
3. Director supervision: monitor queues, progress, failed stages, quality, delays and bottlenecks.
4. Recovery: resume durable checkpoints, retry recoverable failures and prevent duplicate production or publication.
5. Quality oversight: ensure a Director cannot label an incomplete episode as finished.
6. Owner communication: report decisions, blockers, upcoming plans and requests for approval.
7. Analytics: compare genuine performance data and recommend improvements.
8. Business coordination: support approved campaigns, affiliate links, promotions and collaborations.

Hermes should make routine, reversible decisions within policies the owner has approved. It should escalate decisions involving public publishing, new credentials, spending, sensitive content, or other protected actions.

