| AI and media-provider adapters | Research, writing, TTS, visuals and motion                       |
| OAuth and publisher adapters   | Authorized connections and platform-specific publishing          |
| Evidence ledger                | Traceable artifacts, approvals, receipts and QC results          |
| Cloud scheduler and watchdog   | Unattended operation, monitoring and recovery                    |
| Owner dashboard                | Configuration, communication, approvals and oversight            |
| Analytics and optimization     | Learning from verified performance                               |
| Postiz integration             | Optional social scheduling/management through a separate service |

The architecture should be free-first and quota-aware. Open-source tools and permitted local execution should be preferred where practical, with external providers used only when configured and available.

The system must also provide authentication, role-based access control, CSRF protection where applicable, credential isolation, safe migrations, audit logs, backups, monitoring and recovery procedures.

A successful unit test suite is necessary, but it is not sufficient to establish that the cloud system can operate continuously or produce a complete real episode.

