## 12. What counts as a genuinely finished ST Production House?

ST should not be considered fully complete just because the repository builds, tests pass or the dashboard loads.

Use three separate acceptance levels:

Level 1 — Software-complete

The core application, independent Director configuration, durable queues, provider adapters, media pipeline, approval gates, evidence, security and automation pass their required tests.

Level 2 — Live-enabled

Real provider access and account connections work. ST produces genuine media, verifies it, publishes only with authorization, stores real receipts, and ingests official analytics.

Level 3 — Business-operational

The entire system runs reliably in the cloud, recovers from failures, manages multiple Directors independently, produces the canonical package repeatedly, operates approved campaigns, and uses genuine performance data to improve its business.

The final acceptance test should include at least one complete real episode, both independently usable content Shorts/Reels, the separate brand Reel, verified QC evidence, approved publication, genuine receipts, official analytics and demonstrated recovery from a controlled failure. Scaling claims require separate load and isolation evidence.

